        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: પ્રાણી",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "પ્રાણી — prāṇī — \"animal, living creature\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "મેં જંગલમાં ઘણાં પ્રાણી જોયાં. — mẽ jangalmā̃ ghaṇā̃ prāṇī joyā̃ — \"I saw many animals in the forest.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "પ્રાણી (prāṇī) is Sanskrit prāṇin, \"living, a living creature\", built on prāṇa, \"breath of life\", and taken over whole as a learned loan, a tatsama (CDIAL 8932)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for everyday life at A2."
